  <h2>Editorial principles</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No invented certainty.</strong> Every claim is classified: primary source, historical evidence, scholarly interpretation, tradition, research, practitioner experience, or editorial synthesis.</li>
      <li><strong>No hallucinations.</strong> Books, quotations, texts, studies and experiences are never fabricated; legends stay legends.</li>
      <li><strong>Practitioner material is evidence, not content farm filler.</strong> Raw community material is cleaned, anonymized, structured and routed — and only published when it creates, connects, corrects or deepens knowledge.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
